
We are going to re-write the dos.js script, there are no functions using the existing code so nothing needs to be "backwards compatiable", everything in this script is a fresh start. Ignore previous versions of dos.js, let us re-write this script from the ground up to avoid costly bugs and incompatibilities with previous code.

The variables DEVICE= and DOS= have been removed from the qandy8.htm global declarations and are now to be considered local variables. 

I want to remove the "harddrive" and "server" devices along with any routines that use them as it has been decided they are a security threat. Replace them with a "rs232" device which will up the browser's "upload" and "download" functions to save and load files to and from the qandy and the user's harddrive.


  


 

                 
                       Qandy PC DOS:
                       Disk Operating System


             DOS="name" — set to true after user confirms DOS installation, all DOS
                          functions should be inside "if (DOS) {}" checks    

       dosMount(device) — sets the active device to access, default "local" for localStorage
      
          DEVICE="name" — local var for active device
      
        dosBackup(data) — formats active device with JSON strong, if data is omitted
                          returns JSON string with contents of device for backup
     
              dosList() — returns string with list of files separated by new lines
                      
     dosSave(file,data) — saves var data as filename to active device, if filename
                          begins with > (">filename") append data to existing file

          dosLoad(file) — returns contents of filename from active device

    dosCopy(file, dest) — copies file into clipboard for dosPaste command, 
                          if dest is provided it also copies the file into
                          the dest file, returns error if dest already exists
                          
         dosPaste(dest) — pastes the clipboard contents into dest, returns
                          error if dest already exists

  dosRename(file, dest) — renames file to dest 

          dosType(file) — print() file to display screen
            
      dosDownload(file) — triggers browser download file prompt to download file
      
        dosUpload(file) — triggers browser upload file prompt to upload file
      
  
        dosDelete(file) — deletes filename from active device 

        dosExists(file) — returns true if filename exists      



                   name — Name of file, maximum length 255 bytes, allowed
                          characters: A–Z, a–z, 0–9, space (leading/trailing
                          trimmed), minus, underscore, dot (but not first
                          character), parentheses, plus, and equals: -_.()+= 
                       
                   data — plain UTF‑8 text, use base64 for binary data, dos.js
                          returns whole file content as single text string.
                       
                 device — local, harddrive, server, echo, or none.
                 
                          server is not currently implemented, will eventually
                          allow for web based drives such as Google or DropBox.
 
 

